alias
Usage: alias [NAME[=VALUE]]

Give a command a shorter name. With no arguments, list every alias.

	alias ll='ls -l'	define one
	alias ll			show what ll expands to
	alias				list them all

Aliases are expanded only in interactive shells and only as the FIRST word
of a command, so they are a typing convenience, never a scripting tool.
Nothing here persists -- the root is read-only and there is no rc file.

See also: unalias, type, command
